Body:
@kommander since this was assigned to you, could you confirm whether the narrow footer-only scope above is worth a small PR?

I can keep it strictly to live model usage telemetry during active turns: `in`, `out`, and rolling `tok/s`. No shell/tool streaming changes, no plugin/statusline API changes, and final provider usage/cost would remain authoritative.

If maintainers would rather fold this into #8619/#13885 or another existing token/TPS issue, I can follow that direction instead.

@kapilratnani Saw your other comment on the other issue.

I think the /skills command doesnt let the Agent load the skills on its own, it adds thw whole skill to the context, im thining that is more of a manual/deliberate action from the user forcing the skill text in the context.

But in the case of the agent "loading" the skill that seems to still work, if it doesnt for you lease share your config and maybe an example of the skill you are trying to deny and I can check it out and try to repod on my end

i am using this config 
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5",
  "mcp": {
    "docker": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": [
        "npx",
        "-y",
        "@docker/mcp-server"
      ]
    },
    "github": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": [
        "npx",
        "-y",
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"
      ],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_TOKEN": "env:GITHUB_TOKEN"
      }
    },
    "postgres": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": [
        "npx",
        "-y",
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres",
        "postgresql://localhost/mydb"
      ]
    }
  },
  "instructions": [
  ],
  "permission": {
    "skill": {
      "*": "deny",
      "tdd": "allow",
      "vercel-react-best-practices": "allow"
    }
  }
}
```
I tried to trigger a grill-me skill which is installed globally. 
Prompt : "start a grill me session" - did not trigger
Prompt : "/grill-me on this project" - Trigger.

Then i modified the config to allow the grill-me skill:
```
  "permission": {
    "skill": {
      "*": "deny",
     "grill-me": "allow", 
     "tdd": "allow",
      "vercel-react-best-practices": "allow"
    }
  }
```

Prompt : "start a grill me session" - skill loaded.
